        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computer Graphics - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Read this left to right.** A scene (geometry, lights, camera, materials) is\ntransformed into the camera's coordinate frame, the visible surface at each pixel is\ndetermined, that surface is shaded to produce a color, and the result is written to a\nframebuffer and sent to a display. The bracketed numbers point to the guide that owns\neach stage."
    },
